# Source of Truth

## Purpose

Define which files are canonical when documents disagree, so every agent
resolves conflicts the same way and no generation quietly rewrites canon.

## Scope

All layers, all tasks, all phases. Applies to every file under `production/`
and to the generated harness wrappers (`.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.cursor/`,
`.opencode/`, `.agents/`).

## Core Principles

- Bibles and approved masters are canon. Prompts, storyboards, and generated
  media are derived artifacts and MUST be regenerated when canon changes.
- Derived artifacts NEVER feed back into canon implicitly. Promoting a
  generation to canon is an explicit approval act (see `approval-policy.md`).
- Generated directories are write-only for humans: regenerate, never hand-edit.

## Authority Order

When two files disagree, the higher entry wins. Fix the lower one.

1. `production/project.yaml` — project-level facts (title, format, providers).
2. Bibles: `story/story-bible.yaml`, `characters/*/character.yaml` +
   `wardrobe.yaml`, `locations/*/location.yaml` + `map.yaml`, `props/*/prop.yaml`.
3. Approved masters in `production/references/` (`_MASTER` assets) and
   `references/manifest.yaml`.
4. Scene files: `scenes/<SC_ID>/scene.yaml`, `blocking.yaml`, shot files.
5. Continuity state: `continuity/` (authoritative for *observed* state, not
   for intent — intent lives in bibles and scene files).
6. Compiled prompt packages under `prompts/` and `scenes/*/prompts/`.
7. Generated media and records under `generations/`.

## Conflict Resolution

- On conflict, the agent MUST update the lower-authority file to match the
  higher one, then regenerate anything derived from it. It MUST NOT "split the
  difference" or silently pick the newer file.
- If two files at the same tier disagree (e.g. two bibles), the agent MUST
  stop and escalate to human review; it NEVER guesses.
- A prompt that contradicts a bible is a defect in the prompt, even if its
  output looks better. Change the bible first if the new direction is wanted.

## Generated Artifacts

- `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, `.opencode/`, `.agents/` are produced by
  `npm run sync:harnesses`. NEVER hand-edit them; edit the source layer and
  re-run the sync.
- `production/shots/shots.yaml` is a generated index. NEVER edit it directly;
  edit the per-scene shot files and rebuild.
- Compiled prompt packages are outputs of `scripts/compile-prompts.js`. Edit
  bibles, scene files, or reference plans, then recompile.

## Validation

- `scripts/validate.js` schema-checks every structured file and flags prompt
  packages whose source hash no longer matches the current bibles.
- `hooks/validate-after-write.js` re-validates any structured file on write.
- `hooks/protect-approved-assets.js` blocks edits to approved masters.
- Same-tier conflicts and canon changes require human review before work
  continues.
